// M4 of the C++ runtime retirement plan: inbound TLS on the Nova reactor, no Asio. A server coroutine
// terminates a server-side TLS handshake over a reactor-native AsyncStream and serves an HTTP request;
// a client coroutine TLS-connects (reactor-native asyncConnect) and checks the response. The whole
// handshake and data path run on ONE reactor loop. This is the last Asio dependency in the server
// path: App.run now serves TLS on the reactor (serveReactorConn tlsAccepts when useTls is set), so the
// TLS -> Asio fallback is gone. The wolfSSL memory-BIO pump is unchanged; only its transport moved to
// the reactor. Deterministic + self-contained (loopback, embedded self-signed cert).
import assert;
import bytes;
import string;
import os.sys;
import net.reactor;
import net.reactorio;
import net.asyncio;
import net.asynctls;

